(* README *)

1 - Overview
    --------

    P001 formalizes the pigeonhole divisibility theorem over naturals.
    The package-level contract states:

      - for every natural number `n`,
      - for every list `A` of length `n + 1`,
      - if all elements of `A` are pairwise distinct and lie in `1, ..., 2n`,
      - then there exist distinct `a, b in A` such that
        `Nat.divide a b \/ Nat.divide b a`.

    The proof architecture is obligation-driven.
    We first build an odd-part arithmetic layer (2-adic decomposition and
    odd-part bridge), then a finite odd codomain layer, then an abstract
    list-level pigeonhole collision route, and finally a collision-to-
    divisibility bridge.

    The root file `P001__CIC.v` is the package boundary.
    It imports the obligation modules under `CIC__Dependencies/`,
    retains semantic branch obligations as part of the published reference
    surface, and composes the endpoint consumed by `P001__QED.v`.

    The public contract alias lives in `P001__QED.v`.
    The certification layer closes the result by direct reuse of the CIC
    endpoint and exports aggregate assumption artifacts.


